<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept copper imports rise 38.2 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept copper imports rise 38.2 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in September totalled 29,794 tonnes, up 38.2 percent from 21,557 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Sept 96	  Aug 96	  Sept 95</p>
<p> Total	   29,794	   21,211	  21,557</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	   10,129	    8,242	   5,801</p>
<p> U.S.	     4,371	    3,008	   3,394</p>
<p> Zambia	   7,083	    4,329	   2,890</p>
<p>Imports in the first nine months of 1996 were 271,451 tonnes, against 311,164 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
